    fix(namespaces): register creates against the root config; union-list on-disk namespaces (DB-GAP-057)
    
    be129bc (GAP-062) passed the NAMESPACES root as configDir to
    registerNamespace, so every HTTP/MCP namespace create since 09-22 wrote
    its mapping into a stray namespaces/duckbrain.config.json (1.64 MB,
    17473 mappings on this host) instead of the root config. GET
    /api/namespaces reads the root config and never saw those namespaces:
    POST 201 -> immediate GET misses the namespace (auger AUG-051 consumer
    damage: idempotent-create re-POSTs -> 409, 106 pytest setup errors).
    
    - createNamespaceTool now registers + sets default against
      resolveDuckbrainRoot() (the config root); GAP-062 directory placement
      under resolveNamespacesPath() is unchanged.
    - GET /api/namespaces unions a read-only one-shot census of the
      namespaces root under the registry rows: on-disk dirs with no mapping
      become onDiskOnly rows; registry rows with no dir keep
      directoryMissing (REG-GONE-001). Top-level drift {onDiskOnly,
      directoryMissing} counts appear only when non-zero.
    - Regression: namespaces-dbgap057.test.ts (live scratch daemon:
      create-then-list pin, stray-config guard, drift flags/counts, dir
      placement). AGENTS.md count sync 170/1366 -> 171/1372.
    
    Verified live: unit 171/171 files 1372/1372, tsc clean, prettier clean,
    integration 44/44, scratch-daemon AC probes all green.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
